HST Office: Vietnamese exam papers type the text inside MathType equations in legacy 8-bit
fonts: TCVN3 (".VnTime", ".VnTimeH" ...) or VNI ("VNI-Times" ...). The WMF previews keep those
bytes, which were decoded with the system code page and drawn with a substitute font, so
"(rắn)" showed as "(r¾n)", "đặc" as "®Æc" whenever the legacy font is not installed (always on
Linux, often on new Windows/macOS machines), and the PDF text was garbage. WMF text in such a
font is now decoded from TCVN3/VNI (tables from data/vietnamese/encoding-maps.json, generated by
scripts/patches/generate-legacy-vn-font-table.py) and drawn with Times New Roman (Arial for
.VnArial); a VNI letter + tone mark pair keeps the advance of both bytes.

